    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our primary offensive engine. Boasting a team-high efficiency score of 78.75, **Corbin Carroll** is a must-start; despite facing a lefty in Nick Lodolo, his elite sprint speed and a 17% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s high xERA profile override any platoon concerns. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.49) and **Isaac Paredes** (65.97) follow closely as our next strongest options. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits significantly from the platoon advantage against the right-handed Troy Melton, while **Isaac Paredes** leverages a favorable park factor and a solid matchup against J.T. Ginn. Meanwhile, **Gabriel Moreno** continues to hold down the catcher spot with a strong 65.11 rating, buoyed by a prime #3 hole projection and steady recency form.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who fell just short of the lineup with a 47.73 score. While **Cole Young** provides elite stolen base upside\u2014a priority for our roster construction\u2014the unfavorable matchup against the lefty Matthew Boyd, combined with a projected #7 spot in the batting order, lowered his ceiling relative to the starting middle infielders. Elsewhere, **Mickey Moniak** (59.91) and **Josh Naylor** (58.40) narrowly earned starts despite varying platoon pressures. We are closely monitoring the status of **Henry Bolte**, whose 56.01 score is highly sensitive to his lead-off positioning; should he slide down the order, his utility diminishes rapidly. \n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board. While **Corbin Carroll**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Isaac Paredes** are locked in, our reliance on players like **Jose Caballero** (52.47) and **Zach McKinstry** (51.71) is contingent on their specific order placement. We are intentionally holding **Brice Turang** on the bench today, as the matchup against Chris Sale presents a sub-3.00 xERA risk that effectively neutralized his SB-heavy profile. We will continue to evaluate the weather and confirmed lineups to ensure we don\u2019t burn precious game caps on suboptimal pivots.",
